OpenTTD for AmigaOS 3.x (AmiCradle)
===================================

Version @VERSION@.

OpenTTD @UPSTREAM_VERSION@, the open source engine for Transport Tycoon
Deluxe, built for a 68040 or 68060 with an FPU. It draws and plays sound
through GFOpenGPU's SDL2.module. OpenGFX and OpenSFX, the free graphics
and sound sets, are in the drawer, so the game plays as it is.

Requirements
------------

- AmigaOS 3.2, a 68040 or 68060 with an FPU, an RTG screen.
- GFOpenGPU's SDL2.module in LIBS:GFOpenGPU/.
- 64 MB of free Fast RAM; about 60 MB of disk.

Installing
----------

Unpack the archive anywhere (on AmiCradle: SYS:Utilities/OpenCompress x
openttd-...lha RAM:), then double-click Install-OpenTTD beside the
OpenTTD drawer. It asks where the game goes (Work:Games by default) and
keeps your saves and settings when you install over an earlier copy.
If you own Transport Tycoon Deluxe, the Installer can copy its graphics
and sounds in from your own disks or install; they are not needed.

Playing
-------

- Double-click the openttd icon. The game opens its own 640 x 480 screen
  and runs in one task. New games default to 64 x 64 tile maps; bigger
  maps work but are slow on a 68040.
- Saves go to the drawer's save drawer, settings to openttd.cfg.
- SetEnv OPENTTD_LOG 1 writes a log beside the game; OPENTTD_PERF 1 adds
  a line of timings a second.

What this build leaves out
--------------------------

- Network play, the server list and online content (no socket library).
- Music: OpenTTD plays music only through MIDI players this platform has
  not got. Sound effects play.
- Compressed saves: saves are written uncompressed, and saves from other
  builds in a compressed format do not load.

This is a release candidate: it has been built, not yet played through
on a lab. Report problems at https://github.com/DalsinAI/amigaopenttd.

